        "original_id": "0a09d18b-6ccf-515c-b92a-7dd9ca618fc0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Clarence Brown, Peter Glenville, Arthur Arling, Sidney Franklin, Charles Rosher, Leonard Smith\n- Works: The Yearling, Gone with the Wind\n- Organizations: Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer, Academy Awards\n- Topics: film directing, acting, cinematography\n\nFacts:\n- Clarence Brown was born on May 10, 1890, and he was an American film director.\n- Peter Glenville, born Peter Patrick Brabazon Browne, was born on October 28, 1913, and he was an English film and stage actor and director.\n- Arthur Arling's early work included the 1939 film Gone with the Wind.\n- The Yearling is a 1946 Technicolor family film drama about a young boy who adopts a trouble-making young deer.\n- The 1946 film The Yearling was directed by Clarence Brown, produced by Sidney Franklin, and released by Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer.\n- Arthur Arling worked on the 1946 film The Yearling and won a joint Oscar for it with Charles Rosher and Leonard Smith.\n- Peter Glenville died on June 3, 1996.\n- Clarence Brown died on August 17, 1987.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
